# The mtkclient clone is a third-party git repo with its own history. It is
# reproduced by tools/setup-mtkclient.sh, and our two changes to it live in
# vendor/mtkclient-macos-fuse.patch -- which IS tracked.
vendor/mtkclient/

# Device images. A full flash.bin is ~16 GB; even the critical set is tens of
# MB of binary that git would store badly and that must never leave the machine
# by accident -- some of these partitions carry IMEI and calibration data.
backups/

# Android / Gradle
.gradle/
.kotlin/
build/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab

# Release signing. The keystore and the passwords that open it live outside the
# repo entirely; app/build.gradle.kts reads keystore.properties if it is there
# and falls back to an unsigned release build if it is not, so a clone builds
# without them. Losing the keystore means never being able to update the app in
# place again -- an APK signed by a different key will not install over one
# signed by this one -- so it is backed up somewhere that is not this machine.
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties

# JetBrains
.idea/
*.iml

# Design reference photographed on the handset. 1.7 MB, and its own filename
# says it is temporary -- it guides the layout work and is deleted when the UI
# lands, so it is not worth putting in history.
Proof Of Concept Art Reference (Delete At End of Project).png

.DS_Store

# The Magisk patching kit, extracted from the APK by tools/setup-magisk.sh.
# Binary, and reproducible from a pinned checksum, so it is not worth tracking.
vendor/magisk-armeabi-v7a/
